+   * panel that can be short. `dvh` alone was the first attempt and it was not
+   * enough: dvh measures the WINDOW, so on a full-height window it resolved to
+   * ~387px and the palette grew to 374px — covering essentially the whole chat
+   * area above the composer. The panel can be a fraction of the window, and the
+   * list should be sized by the room it actually has.
+   *
+   * 340px stays the ceiling; the `48%` of the panel height below is the tighter
+   * of the two whenever the panel is short, which is exactly when the old
+   * behaviour hurt. `dvh` remains as the window-level backstop.
    */
